{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1744219,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"Aqua Clean","festival_id":504454,"organization_id":675999,"web_url":"www.techfest26.com\/package","start_date":"2026-09-03T13:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-16T13:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/aqua-clean-techfest26-annual-technical-festival-of-sliet-sant-longowal-institute-of-engineering-and-technol-1744219","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>AQUA-CLEAN:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Introduction:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>AQUA-CLEAN is a sustainability-driven event challenging participants to design and build a functional water filtration model using limited and easily available materials.<\/li>\n<li>The goal is to simulate a real-world water purification problem in low-resource settings.<\/li>\n<li>The event combines innovation, awareness, and practical engineering.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to all Diploma, UG, and PG students from any branch or discipline from recognised colleges or universities.<\/li>\n<li>All participants must carry a valid college ID card during the event for verification.<\/li>\n<li>Failure to produce a valid college ID may lead to disqualification.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Problem Statement:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants must design a water treatment system for a village of 500 people facing contaminated groundwater, unreliable electricity, limited technical expertise, limited maintenance budget, agricultural wastewater, and seasonal water availability.<\/li>\n<li>The system should produce safe water while generating minimal secondary waste.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must develop a strategy for recovering or reusing contaminants or treatment materials.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Constraints:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>No grid electricity.<\/li>\n<li>Limited transportation.<\/li>\n<li>Limited to no chemicals.<\/li>\n<li>Must be portable.<\/li>\n<li>Must be deployable quickly.<\/li>\n<li>Must treat variable contamination.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Components Required:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sand.<\/li>\n<li>Gravel.<\/li>\n<li>Charcoal.<\/li>\n<li>Cotton.<\/li>\n<li>Mesh\/cloth.<\/li>\n<li>PET bottles or containers.<\/li>\n<li>Funnels.<\/li>\n<li>Rubber bands and plastic pipes.<\/li>\n<li>Tape\/glue and other approved materials.<\/li>\n<li>Chemical filters, electrical equipment, and UV treatment are not allowed.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Team size: 1&ndash;3 members.<\/li>\n<li>Time limit: 2 hours to design and demonstrate the model.<\/li>\n<li>Only approved materials can be used.<\/li>\n<li>Contaminated water will be provided by the organisers.<\/li>\n<li>Final water must be visibly clear and measurable.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Water Clarity: 30%.<\/li>\n<li>Design Innovation: 25%.<\/li>\n<li>Material Usage: 15%.<\/li>\n<li>Presentation: 15%.<\/li>\n<li>Filtration Speed: 15%.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rewards &amp; Recognition:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Exciting prizes for the Top 3 Winners.<\/li>\n<li>Certificates for all participants.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Certification Policy:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All participants will receive certificates.<\/li>\n<li>Winners will be awarded certificates and prizes based on the final results declared by the judges.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Important Note:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Judges' decisions will be final and binding.<\/li>\n<li>Inappropriate or unsafe behaviour will lead to disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Use of non-approved or unsafe materials will result in penalties.<\/li>\n<li>Participants may prepare their water purification system in advance or at the venue, as per their convenience.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must report 15 minutes before the event starts.<\/li>\n<li>The organisers reserve the right to modify the rules, schedule, or any aspect of the event with prior notice.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must stay updated through official notices posted on the SLIET techFEST 2026 website.<\/li>\n<li>Further modifications to the problem statement may be made based on subsequent analysis and requirements.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Registration for the&nbsp;techFEST&rsquo;26 package&nbsp;is compulsory for&nbsp;accommodation and&nbsp;other perks, while&nbsp;participation in individual&nbsp;events is free*.<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><a href=\"http:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/\">www.techfest26.com<\/a><\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>For Further Query:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Domain Advisor: Raju Kumar &ndash; 2341023\/GCS, 6209681064.<\/li>\n<li>Domain Coordinator: Aisha Kumari &ndash; 2442003\/GCT, 6209681064.<\/li>\n<li>Event Coordinator: Gurleen Kaur &ndash; 254014007\/GCT, 6209681064.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":null,"registration_clicks":0,"user_id":27463276,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-08-25T22:02:31+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-05T00:21:43+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"rNIb08s","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":0,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":2,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":77,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-08-27 03:57:11","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_automation":false,"auto_send_participa